From ccca622cfac73799378c84997624483af9665f9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ohgur <ohgurlabs@github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:58:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] hipGraph: propagate UpdateAQLPacket failure out of
 hipGraphExecUpdate

hipGraphExecUpdate's bulk update loop assigns UpdateAQLPacket()'s error to
'status' without checking it and falls through to HIP_RETURN(hipSuccess).
Under device-memory exhaustion the packet re-capture legitimately fails
(with the checks from PR #10022); the exec keeps the previously captured
packet and the next launch executes it: silent wrong output, and with
kernarg-pool recycling eventually a malformed AQL packet (CP fault + queue
abort observed on gfx1100). All other UpdateAQLPacket call sites already
propagate their status.

Surface the failure as hipErrorGraphExecUpdateFailure with hErrorNode_out
and hipGraphExecUpdateError set, matching the SetParams failure paths in
the same function. Frameworks that destroy and re-instantiate on this code
(llama.cpp/ggml) recover in place; validated on gfx1100 against the
therock-7.14 tag: 32 deep inference runs with zero crashes or output
corruption, and a recovery probe verifying 102,600 consecutive bit-exact
launches across 25 destroy/re-instantiate cycles at 0 MiB free.

Related: #10021, #10022
---
 projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp b/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
index 3d57a19f2c..9692831f85 100644
--- a/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/hipamd/src/hip_graph.cpp
@@ -2830,6 +2830,17 @@ hipError_t hipGraphExecUpdate(hipGraphExec_t hGraphExec, hipGraph_t hGraph,
         auto graphExec = reinterpret_cast<hip::GraphExecBase*>(hGraphExec);
         if (newGraphNodes[i]->GraphCaptureEnabled()) {
           status = graphExec->UpdateAQLPacket(reinterpret_cast<hip::GraphKernelNode*>(oldGraphExecNodes[i]));
+          if (status != hipSuccess) {
+            // A packet re-capture failure (e.g. kernarg allocation under device-memory
+            // exhaustion) leaves the exec holding the previously captured packet.
+            // Reporting success here makes the next launch execute that stale packet:
+            // silent wrong output, and with kernarg-pool recycling a malformed AQL
+            // packet (see issue #10021). Surface the failure instead, matching the
+            // SetParams failure paths above.
+            *hErrorNode_out = reinterpret_cast<hipGraphNode_t>(newGraphNodes[i]);
+            *updateResult_out = hipGraphExecUpdateError;
+            HIP_RETURN(hipErrorGraphExecUpdateFailure);
+          }
         }
       }
     } else {
